{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "095J", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:de459ba68323e6f2112e0cc1249e3ca766c3bc6e9aadf31bf9d7c956e6278839", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSome lemmas that are useful for proving functoriality properties\nof constructible sheaves.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2cb8f26e0a9b29ca2a092b1f3f47db462e33061ccda53abffc600dc2ebc2b209", "unit_id": "tag:095J:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "095J", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$X = \\coprod_i X_i$", "MATH_0003": "$X_i \\times_X U \\to X_i$", "MATH_0004": "$i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-stratified-finite}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1c32b966b6f4b7c69744fd96f4b4fa067fda8b898eb10c30919d9a13de8d7ead", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3fe7ca4469efc276f682449bb165e18080292485944cc28aaf834e662e549f9c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism of quasi-compact and quasi-separated\nschemes (for example an <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism of Noetherian schemes). Then there\nexists a partition <MATH_0002> by constructible locally closed\nsubschemes such that <MATH_0003> is finite <ACCENT_0003>tale for all <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b14ff6610a67ee15b1347d070723664f24e070bcd29ebfc7e9f0fee5faba4658", "unit_id": "tag:03S0:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "095J", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U = \\bigcup U_j$", "MATH_0004": "$U_j \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$U_j \\cap U_{j'} \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$X = \\coprod X_i$", "MATH_0007": "$X_i$", "MATH_0008": "$i$", "MATH_0009": "$V = U \\times_X X_i$", "MATH_0010": "$V_j = U_j \\times_X X_i \\to X_i$", "MATH_0011": "$V_{jj'} = (U_j \\cap U_{j'}) \\times_X X_i \\to X_i$", "MATH_0012": "$V_j$", "MATH_0013": "$V_{jj'}$", "MATH_0014": "$V_{jj'} \\subset V_j$", "MATH_0015": "$V_{jj'} \\to X_i$", "MATH_0016": "$V = \\bigcup V_j$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{O}(V_j) \\to \\mathcal{O}(V_{jj'})$", "MATH_0018": "$V \\to X_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-stratify-flat-fp-qf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-image-proper-scheme-closed}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-characterize-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:11006e657c498f2878d251d3a14104cc0c406444e370c900d03b9af2cf97eec9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e3bb6ed8d952c27b6ad7177996fe40b89682ad6be4b1cf4fb7054a035b253ad0", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is separated, then this is\nMore on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nIn general, we may assume <MATH_0002> is affine. Choose a finite affine open\ncovering <MATH_0003>. Apply the previous case to all the morphisms\n<MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> and choose a common\nrefinement <MATH_0006> of the resulting partitions.\nAfter refining the partition further we may assume <MATH_0007> affine as well.\nFix <MATH_0008> and set <MATH_0009>. The morphisms\n<MATH_0010> and\n<MATH_0011> are finite <ACCENT_0001>tale.\nHence <MATH_0012> and <MATH_0013> are affine schemes and <MATH_0014>\nis closed as well as open (since <MATH_0015> is proper, so\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>\napplies). Then <MATH_0016> is separated because\n<MATH_0017> is surjective, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nThus the previous case applies to <MATH_0018> and we can further\nrefine the partition if needed (it actually isn't but we don't\nneed this).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aa1d8d31155c61be9cf830a007aa89fd07a4465623e5fe52549f0755ba78a8e5", "unit_id": "tag:03S0:proof"}
